<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <!--
    The Intl library of the shared JavaScript libraries programme (milestone SJL-9.3; Broiler.VM's
    decision JSD-0082 and its decisions D8, D9 and D18 to D22): the ECMA-402 algorithms over the
    locale data an engine hands in, ported from Broiler.VM's JavaScript profile stage by stage, in the
    order a to e of the area design (decision D3). It names neither engine and reads no culture.

    Stage SJL-9.3a's skeleton (the plan's task 5.0) holds the data contract of decision D8 in its two
    layers: the tables as an IIntlDataSet, whose IntlTable keeps Broiler.VM's JsIntlTable numbers,
    decoded once per process by the decoders Broiler.VM's JsIntlTables holds; and the questions as an
    ILocaleData, which the decoder implementation answers from the tables and CompositeLocaleData
    orders - the shared data, then an optional secondary provider, then the locale's parent and root.
    It also holds the statuses that replace the engines' errors. Every later stage adds its sub-area's
    algorithms over that contract.

    Stage SJL-9.3a's sub-area (a) (the plan's task 5.a): locale identifiers (LocaleId), negotiation
    (LocaleNegotiation), the Intl.Locale constructor's steps (LocaleRecord), Locale info (LocaleInfo)
    and Intl.supportedValuesOf (SupportedValues), ported from Broiler.VM's JsLocaleTag and its realm's
    Intl, Locale and supportedValuesOf code at 4cf9ca44, with ASCII casing (decision D19), statuses for
    its errors, the caller's WorkCharge (decision D18) and rows L9 and L18 corrected (decision D32).

    References (decision D9; architecture section 2's "Algorithms, Unicode; data through a provider
    interface"): Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms, whose WorkCharge every input-growing path takes
    (decision D18), and Broiler.Unicode.Algorithms. No engine, nothing of Broiler.VM, and no table:
    each engine embeds its own, which this library reads through the provider (SJL-D-6 (c)).

    NOT PACKED YET. Decision D29 publishes one stream version that carries the complete library, and
    the plan's stage SJL-9.3f packs it; until then the package identity is set and nothing is packed,
    so that no stream version carries a part of it.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Broiler.ECMAScript.Intl</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Broiler.ECMAScript.Intl</AssemblyName>
    <PackageId>Broiler.ECMAScript.Intl</PackageId>
    <Description>The Intl algorithms shared by the Broiler JavaScript engines (ECMA-402), over the locale data an engine hands in: the data contract (the generated tables as an IIntlDataSet, decoded once into the question-level ILocaleData, with CompositeLocaleData ordering the shared data, an optional secondary provider, and the locale's parent and root), the statuses that replace engine errors, and locale identifiers, negotiation, Intl.Locale's record, Locale info and supportedValuesOf.</Description>
    <PackageTags>broiler;ecmascript;javascript;shared;intl;ecma-402;cldr</PackageTags>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms\Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms.csproj" />
    <PackageReference Include="Broiler.Unicode.Algorithms" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The tests call the table text readers, internal to the decoder implementation, directly. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Broiler.ECMAScript.Intl.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
